ur shift, you'll come across people . Those compactor rooms full of trash will still be there in a few minutes; There's no rush. </p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3879130/extras/876d40f9cfc792e006cba28093bd2d5d.avif?t=1756134017\" width=616 height=100 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><i><strong>Each floor possesses a compactor room. Remove anything that you find inside of it</strong></i></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You'll be tackling one of the apartment complexes<i> of<strong> BLOC C</strong></i>, a festering obelisk of brick and plaster that houses the worst of the worst. At least, that's how any average <i>Eckhart Citizen</i> would describe it.  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3879130/extras/7e26165a7afe677195007f9f0542e02d.avif?t=1756134017\" width=616 height=100 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><i><strong>Repel enemies as you ascend the building so you can continue your work</strong></i></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >After <i>The Haze</i>, life changed in ways humanity couldn't have imagined. <strong><i>Anglers</i></strong> are chief among them. Little is known about these phantoms save for their unrelenting desire to erase us. Thankfully, <i>Eckhart Resources &amp; Acquisitions</i> has leveraged their proprietary technology to make existence possible again.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3879130/extras/0c84b7803eec65d97ccc1e75bcd84618.avif?t=1756134017\" width=616 height=100 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><i><strong>Conversate with tenants and learn more about the world</strong></i></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A hundred floors is no small feat. Throughout your shift, yo